Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Epilogue", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.97931385274067*^9, 
  3.979313855292756*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"fcc3f51d-8732-425c-9486-\
4d4f3cc28ee7"],

Cell["\<\
We began this quest with a mysterious artifact : a Visualizer that produced \
beautiful, chaotic orbits but whose inner workings were a riddle . \
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9793138614064703`*^9, 3.979313873682032*^9}, 
   3.9794331329125967`*^9},ExpressionUUID->"570460fa-e00a-4141-ae60-\
eada39ee1a54"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The Wizard Chandra warned us that the machinery\[LongDash]the Kerr metric\
\[LongDash]was too complex to understand by force. He was right. Confronting \
the dragon (the ",
 StyleBox["ab\[NoBreak]-\[NoBreak]initio",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " vacuum equations) earned us firethorns of algebra. But, we retreated only \
from the blaze, not from the quest. Consulting the Wizard' s Map (the \
linearized limit), we were sure that the keys lay ahead. We assembled the \
Magical Sword (the Ernst Equation) from provisions carried by our faithful \
squire, the \[ScriptCapitalU]\[ScriptCapitalD] Toolkit. With that sword, we \
pierced the thicket and found the enchanting jewels to pacify the dragon. The \
terrifying complexity of the spinning black hole\[LongDash]the \
frame-dragging, the time dilation, the time-azimuth \
coupling\[LongDash]collapses into a single, elegant identity  The Rip Tide of \
the Ergosphere is not a glitch, it is twisting spacetime. We showed that our \
faithful \[ScriptCapitalU]\[ScriptCapitalD] squire is strong enough and that \
our tools are sharp enough for whatever monsters lie ahead. "
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9793138614064703`*^9, 3.9793138643547983`*^9}, {
  3.9793140542716208`*^9, 3.9793144121631117`*^9}, {3.979314442769464*^9, 
  3.979314575683525*^9}, {3.979433151360948*^9, 3.979433272744735*^9}, {
  3.9794638066756363`*^9, 
  3.979463900183309*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"c394089a-75ce-4a64-a5de-\
6a9d192b42a1"]
}, Open  ]],

